==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*5 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 16~16.67 seconds<sup>480f~500f</sup>.
*5 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 4 seconds<sup>120f</sup>, delay 16~16.67 seconds<sup>480f~500f</sup>.
*5 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 4.67 seconds<sup>140f</sup>, delay 16~16.67 seconds<sup>480f~500f</sup>.
*5 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 5.33 seconds<sup>160f</sup>, delay 16~16.67 seconds<sup>480f~500f</sup>.
*5 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 6 seconds<sup>180f</sup>, delay 16~16.67 seconds<sup>480f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Squire Rel]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Le'Behemoth]] spawns as the boss.
**20 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
**3 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
**2 [[Mooth]]s spawn, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
**1 [[R.Ost]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The majority of this stage's difficulty comes from the R.Ost. Killing the R.Ost, ideally as quickly as possible, is thus the top priority. Money is luckily not an issue due to the presence of Mooth and the generous start up. A shield piercer makes the cleanup phase much easier.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] - Great for dealing large chunks out of R.Ost's health, and is spammable enough to kill it within reasonable time. A level 38 Hitman gets a guaranteed knockback on R.Ost every 2 hits, making stalling it and gaining ground much easier. They can also deal reasonable chip damage to Condemned Peng and Mooth.
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] - Paired with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|erasers]], Haniwa can create a near-impenetrable defense against R.Ost, allowing attackers like Hitman to land easy damage without fear of retaliation. They work best at level 42 or higher, as past that threshold, they survive 3 hits from R. Ost. They can be replaced with [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] if need be.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] - The perfect unit for the start and cleanup. Slime is able to easily clear the waves of Cerberus Kids at the beginning of the level, making stalling for money amazingly easy. They're also very useful for cleaning up any remaining Mooths or Condemned Pengs after R.Ost is dead, using Le'Behemoth as a stepping stone.
*[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] - Surprisingly, Cyborg does just fine on this stage. With a good defense, she'll be able to clear both the Condemned Pengs and R.Ost in a short amount of time, assuming you spam her a lot. Using her will eventually cause you to run out of money, but the Condemned Pengs do provide some cashflow to aid in this. However, if you have Hitman, you probably don't need to be using Cyborg.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Like with many other stages, BahaBlast is able to sweep this stage and much of its difficulty. Luring the R.Ost to your base, then chaining it with Bahamut will quickly take down much of its health (2/3rds with just two hit+Explosion combos) and delete much of the stage's difficulty. If you have difficulty with Bahamut chaining, the [[Ototo Corps|Thunderbolt Cannon]] can help a lot.

